=== layout: section

# How to Get the Recombination Frequency? (Derivation)

=== layout: one-panel

# Observed Recombination Frequency

@body

- TT tetrads contain two recombinant spores out of four.
- NPD tetrads contain four recombinant spores out of four.
- TT and NPD below are counts; N is the total tetrads.

$$
RF = \frac{\frac{1}{2}TT + NPD}{N} \times 100\%
$$

=== layout: one-panel

# Recombination and Map Distance

@body

- RF correctly measures the fraction of recombinant spores.
- It can underestimate map distance because some crossovers restore parental combinations.
- Unordered tetrad classes let us estimate a correction for double crossovers.

